:PNLGRP.
.*
:HELP name='DSPSRC/ALL'.
:IMHELP name=DSPSRC.
:IMHELP name='DSPSRC/OBJ       '.
:IMHELP name='DSPSRC/OBJTYPE   '.
:IMHELP name='DSPSRC/DSPMOD    '.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für den Befehl
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='DSPSRC'.
Display Source Code (DSPSRC) - Help
:P.
The DSPSRC command is used to display the source member that
contains the source code the object was created from.
.*
:P.
For ILE objects with multiple modules, the DSPSRC command displays
the list of modules to select the one to open.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort OBJ
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DSPSRC/OBJ       '.
Obcekt - Help
:XH3.Object (OBJ)
:P.
Specifies the name an library of the object for which the
source member is to be displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.object-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the object.
:EPARML.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched
until the first match is found.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the library to be searched.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort OBJTYPE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DSPSRC/OBJTYPE   '.
Object type - Help
:XH3.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.
Specifies the type of the object for which the source member is to be
displayed. For a complete list of object types, position the cursor on
the field for the :HP2.Object type:EHP2. (parameter OBJTYPE), and press
F4.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.object-type:EPV.
:PD.Specify the value for the type of object for which the
source member is displayed.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort DSPMOD
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DSPSRC/DSPMOD    '.
Display ILE module list - Help
:XH3.Display ILE module list (DSPMOD)
:P.
Specifies wwhether the list of modules of a ILE program is displayed
or not. If a ILE program only consists of one module, then by default
the list is not displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The module list is not displayed, if the program consists of one
module only.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The module list is displayed.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*====================================================================
.*  Textbausteine, die an mehreren Stellen im Hilfetext
.*  verwendet werden.
.*====================================================================

.*=====================================
.*  Erforderlicher Parameter
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/REQPARM'.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
:EHELP.

.*=====================================
.*  Optionaler Parameter
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
This is an optional parameter.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
:EHELP.

.*=====================================
.*  Werteliste
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/VALUES'.
:P.
The possible values are:
:EHELP.
.*
:EPNLGRP.
